From b864256f80910024fe244698057c15195667df8a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: James Almer <jamrial@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 19 Oct 2024 16:33:58 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] fate: compare decoded output across zlib implementations

Adapt the sample-free part of James Almer's proposal to FFmpeg 9.0.2.
The PDV and seek extensions are local additions.
PDV uses deflate in FFmpeg 9.0.2.
Keep decoded hashes and error checks. Preserve transcode's tenth
argument for the final muxer and use the eleventh for file checksums.
For PDV seeking, compare return values and timestamps without requiring
compression-specific byte positions and packet sizes. Other seek tests
retain these byte checks.

Source: https://ffmpeg.org/pipermail/ffmpeg-devel/2024-October/335181.html
Upstream-Status: Pending

Signed-off-by: James Almer <jamrial@gmail.com>
---
